{"id": "EUVD-2026-95905", "enisaUuid": "0c7194c7-3956-3ca0-9a94-92365589b1bb", "description": "Pingvin Share X from 0.19.0 before 1.22.0 contains an improper authentication vulnerability that allows remote unauthenticated attackers to take over accounts by abusing automatic OAuth email linking in OAuthService.signUp(). Attackers can register a victim's unverified email on an enabled OAuth/OIDC provider, exploiting the missing email_verified check in GenericOidcProvider, to sign in as the victim including administrators while bypassing TOTP.", "datePublished": "2026-10-09T16:04:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-09T17:14:05", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/smp46/pingvin-share-x/security/advisories/GHSA-wrcg-4874-45p7", "https://github.com/smp46/pingvin-share-x/commit/07aa8c0a96030c439e9018ce94a2778bd37304e6", "https://github.com/smp46/pingvin-share-x/blob/de7ffecf9bfc4976993149a5c4c98efe35161424/backend/src/oauth/oauth.service.ts#L158-L175", "https://github.com/smp46/pingvin-share-x/releases/tag/v1.22.0", "https://github.com/smp46/pingvin-share-x", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/pingvin-share-x-0.19.0-before-1.22.0-account-takeover-via-oauth-email-linking"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108157", "GHSA-7p7c-6qwr-q8j7"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.54, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "810141d3-cd02-3d7c-9625-531bcb7869ad", "product": {"name": "pingvin-share-x", "vendor": {"name": "smp46"}}, "product_version": "0.19.0 <1.22.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7633201f-6d48-35de-9c33-baa23746ad8e", "vendor": {"name": "smp46"}}], "isExploited": false}